      "lineNbr": 1166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-18T14:17:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d agree there\u0027s still a use-case for one-off resolveService, as the race between \"service info received\" and \"connect to service host/port\" is there in any case and apps can also retry the whole process in case of failure there. But we might still want to deprecate resolveService (this overload doesn\u0027t have an Executor, and currently doesn\u0027t support receiving multiple service addresses; although that could be fixed). In any case I think this should be in a separate change though.",
      "parentUuid": "d6619f9f_a105d799",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1166,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 1166,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "a317e7478b59289c7cb387b03ef632d9553eb0de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a61d78e9_05f40273",
        "filename": "framework-t/src/android/net/nsd/NsdManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1166,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-19T02:23:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Deprecation should depend on whether we think apps should still use the old method. My understanding of this is : no, we think apps should no longer use the old method ; they should use the new one and be told of any change. Yes, there is still a race, but you\u0027ll be told about it immediately. I do not see a use case where you want to know about a service but you don\u0027t care that it changes.\n\nIf we\u0027re going to deprecate this my preference is to deprecate it in this patch, because it\u0027s a lot clearer for reviewers why and how we\u0027re doing this. I\u0027m willing to approve the deprecation as a followup if that\u0027s not realistic though.",
      "parentUuid": "1f6206b3_11f6a080",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1166,
        "startChar": 16,
